{"id": "28B-76", "cog": 3, "sci": "ok", "key": "ok", "scope": "in", "topic": "ok", "d": "ok", "distractors": "ok", "feedback": "good", "hint": "good", "figure": "ok", "dup": "28B-34", "calc": "na", "action": "REPLACE", "defects": ["exact duplicate of 28B-34: same reaction/question and same four choices (only stem wording/topic tag differ); both could appear in one exam"], "rewrite": {"t": "alcohols", "d": 3, "k": 0, "q": "Diethyl carbonate, (CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>O)<sub>2</sub>C=O, is treated with excess C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>MgBr in ether, then H<sub>3</sub>O<sup>+</sup>. What is the main organic product besides ethanol?", "c": ["triphenylmethanol, (C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>)<sub>3</sub>COH", "benzophenone, (C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>)<sub>2</sub>C=O", "ethyl benzoate, C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>CO<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>3</sub>", "diphenylmethanol, (C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>)<sub>2</sub>CHOH"], "h": "A carbonate carbon carries two OR leaving groups. How many times can a Grignard add before no leaving group is left?", "w": "The first PhMgBr adds and expels ethoxide, giving ethyl benzoate. The ester is more reactive than the carbonate, so it adds a second PhMgBr and expels ethoxide again, giving benzophenone. The ketone is more reactive still and adds a third. Workup gives <b>triphenylmethanol</b>, a 3° alcohol whose three phenyl groups all came from the Grignard.", "x": ["", "Benzophenone is an intermediate; it is more electrophilic than the carbonate and the ester, so excess PhMgBr adds to it.", "Ethyl benzoate is the first intermediate; with excess Grignard it reacts twice more.", "A secondary alcohol needs an H on the carbinol carbon (from a formate ester or a hydride); every group added here is phenyl."]}}
